# EOS Session 0, phase B: declared before anything else lands (INCEPTION.md).
#
# Normalise every text file to LF in the REPOSITORY. Working copies on Windows
# still check out CRLF; this fixes only what is stored, so the tree stops
# depending on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Verified safe when added: `git ls-files --eol` reported zero files stored with
# CRLF, so this declares the behaviour the repo already had rather than
# renormalising anything. Every commit in the 2026-07 rebuild session warned
# about LF/CRLF conversion because the policy was undeclared, not because it was
# wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must use LF so bash on Linux/macOS does not see stray CR.
*.sh text eol=lf
